From: rhythmcache <153998419+rhythmcache@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: call susfs_set_batch_sid() in out_flush for 5.4

In apply_kernelsu_rules(), the call to susfs_set_batch_sid() was placed
inside `#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 10, 0)`.
On Linux 5.4, the function takes the `#else` branch where
susfs_set_batch_sid() was omitted at `out_flush:`. As a result,
susfs_zygote_sid remained 0, causing ksu_handle_setresuid() to fail zygote
identification and skip ksu_install_fd() for the manager app.

Call susfs_set_batch_sid() at out_flush: on Linux 5.4 after the policy
lock is released and the AVC cache is reset.

Pinned to SukiSU commit: de9bc7e6b46181f8b27ac7b96db946420838dd18
Re-check this patch if the SukiSU submodule pin changes.
---
 kernel/selinux/rules.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/selinux/rules.c b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
--- a/kernel/selinux/rules.c
+++ b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
@@ -256,4 +256,7 @@ do_stop_machine:
 out_flush:
     smp_mb();
     reset_avc_cache();
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS
+    susfs_set_batch_sid();
+#endif
 #endif
-- 
